  "id": "Compound::DB00334 - Gene::147",
  "verbalization": "Olanzapine is implicated in the interaction with Adra1b through a shared pathway involving the Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity. The evidence suggests that Olanzapine binds to Adra1a, which then participates in Alpha-adrenergic receptor activity, ultimately being participated by Adra1b. This indicates a potential functional link between Olanzapine and Adra1b, where the drug may influence the activity of the Alpha-adrenergic receptor through Adra1a. The overlapping roles of Adra1a and Adra1b in the Alpha-adrenergic receptor pathway suggest that Olanzapine could modulate the activity of Adra1b, possibly through a mechanism involving the activation of the Alpha-adrenergic receptor. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Olanzapine in regulating the function of Adra1b, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct interaction.",
